window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-5d0a94de49bd5694"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"use-apiprovider-credentials-through-a-gateway\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"api\">通过网关使用 API / 提供商凭据</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用组织提供的网关 URL、模型别名，以及凭据或令牌解析程序，将 Codex 连接到大语言模型（LLM）网关。</p> <p>如果要保留网关并使用 ChatGPT 工作区登录，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597\">通过网关使用 ChatGPT 登录</a>。</p> <p>如需在整个组织范围内推广，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">部署网关</a>。所需 API 行为请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性</a>。如需不经网关直接连接 Bedrock，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">Amazon Bedrock</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"check-for-an-existing-configuration\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">检查是否已有配置</h2> <p>添加配置前，请先确认管理员是否已为你配置 Codex。</p> <ul> <li><strong>CLI：</strong>检查当前选用的配置文件，并运行 <code>codex doctor</code>。启动后，使用 <code>/status</code> 确认当前模型和提供商。</li> <li><strong>macOS 应用：</strong>检查 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>，或组织下发的托管配置。</li> <li><strong>Windows 应用：</strong>检查 <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\config.toml</code>，或组织下发的系统配置。</li> </ul> <p>如果预期的网关提供商和模型已经处于启用状态，请继续<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=verify-the-connection\">验证连接</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"get-your-gateway-connection-details\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">获取网关连接信息</h2> <p>请安装组织批准的 <a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a> 或桌面应用。如果要自行配置 Codex，请向网关团队获取以下信息：</p> <ul> <li>HTTPS 网关基础 URL（包括 API 路径），例如 <code>https://gateway.example.com/v1</code>。</li> <li>要使用的模型名称和提供商 ID。</li> <li>具有适当作用域的网关凭据及其环境变量，或已安装的令牌解析程序及其配置。</li> <li>如有要求，提供模型目录 URL，或目录文件及其本地绝对路径。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"configure-the-provider\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">配置提供商</h2> <p>在 macOS 或 Linux 上，请打开配置文件 <code>config.toml</code>，路径为 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>；在 Windows 上，请打开 <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\config.toml</code>。</p> <p>将此示例合并到现有配置中，并用管理员提供的值替换 URL 和模型。不要重复定义已有的键或表。示例使用 <code>gpt-6-sol</code>；只有管理员确认你的 Codex 版本识别此模型，且随附的元数据与网关相符时，才可在不使用自定义目录的情况下使用它。</p> <p>请将 <code>model</code>、<code>model_provider</code>、<code>model_catalog_json</code> 和 <code>web_search</code> 放在第一个 TOML 表之前。写在表标题之后的键属于该表，因此 Codex 不会将它们读取为顶层设置。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"gpt-6-sol\"\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise-gateway\"\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]\nname = \"Organization Gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/v1\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\nenv_key = \"CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY\"\n</code></pre> <p>如果管理员提供了目录 URL，请将其添加到现有的 <code>[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]</code> 表中：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_catalog_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/codex/models.json\"\n</code></pre> <p>请移除任何当前生效的 <code>model_catalog_json</code> 设置，因为它的优先级高于 URL。管理员可在 <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=serve-a-remote-catalog\">远程目录设置</a>中查看端点要求。</p> <p>如果管理员提供了本地模型目录文件，请保存该文件，并在第一个 TOML 表之前添加 <code>model_catalog_json</code>，其值使用文件的绝对路径。自定义别名需要匹配的目录元数据。例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_catalog_json = \"/etc/codex/gateway-models.json\"\n</code></pre> <p>请使用管理员一并提供的模型名称和目录。只有当文件确实存在于指定位置时，才添加目录路径。</p> <p><code>enterprise-gateway</code> is an illustrative provider ID. Use the same ID in <code>model_provider</code>, <code>[model_providers.&lt;id&gt;]</code>, and <code>[model_providers.&lt;id&gt;.auth]</code>. 此示例会在初次连接测试期间禁用网页搜索；启用前应由管理员确认网关支持此功能。</p> <p>请使用组织的机密信息分发机制，让启动 Codex 的进程能够从环境中读取网关凭据 <code>CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY</code>。不要把凭据写入 TOML 文件或代码仓库。在终端中设置的变量可能无法被从桌面启动的应用读取。</p> <p><a id=\"use-a-custom-authentication-header\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">使用自定义身份验证标头</h3> <p>如果网关要求使用 <code>X-API-Key</code> 等标头，而不是 Bearer 令牌，请将提供商表中的 <code>env_key</code> 替换为：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">env_http_headers = { \"X-API-Key\" = \"CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY\" }\n</code></pre> <p>请使用管理员提供的准确标头名称。Codex 会从指定的环境变量读取其值；不要将凭据写入配置文件。更多信息请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>中的 <code>model_providers.&lt;id&gt;.env_http_headers</code>.</p> <p>如果自定义标头是唯一的身份验证方式，请使用 <code>model_catalog_json</code>；此时不会执行远程目录发现。</p> <p><a id=\"use-an-organization-credential-helper\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">使用组织凭据助手</h3> <p>如果管理员提供了基于命令的身份验证，请使用其安装的助手及配置，而不是 <code>env_key</code>。不要同时配置这两种机制。助手必须已安装在你的计算机上；Codex 不会替你安装。比如，可将示例中的 <code>env_key</code> 设置替换为下表，并使用管理员提供的解析程序路径和参数：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[model_providers.enterprise-gateway.auth]\ncommand = \"/usr/local/bin/fetch-codex-gateway-token\"\nargs = [\"print-token\"]\ntimeout_ms = 30000\nrefresh_interval_ms = 300000\n</code></pre> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">自定义提供商身份验证参考</a> 中说明了命令、参数、超时时间、刷新间隔和令牌输出约定。如果助手无法再获取令牌，请向管理员咨询如何续期登录。</p> <p>助手可执行文件和目录文件都应使用解析后的绝对路径。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-the-cli\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"cli\">配置 CLI</h3> <p>在 macOS 或 Linux 上，CLI 默认读取 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>。保存提供商设置后，运行 <code>codex</code>。在 WSL 中，除非 <code>CODEX_HOME</code> 指向其他位置，否则请使用 Linux 配置和路径。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-the-macos-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"macos\">配置 macOS 应用</h3> <p>macOS 应用读取同一个 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>。保存提供商设置后，请重新启动应用。如果凭据使用环境变量，请确保应用进程可以读取该变量。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-the-windows-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"windows\">配置 Windows 应用</h3> <p>将提供商设置写入 <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\config.toml</code>，然后重新启动应用。对于基于命令的身份验证，请使用管理员安装的解析程序。例如，将 Unix 身份验证表替换为：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[model_providers.enterprise-gateway.auth]\ncommand = 'C:\\Program Files\\OpenAI\\Codex\\fetch-codex-gateway-token.exe'\nargs = [\"print-token\"]\ntimeout_ms = 30000\nrefresh_interval_ms = 300000\n</code></pre> <p>在 Windows TOML 中，单引号括起的字面字符串会保留反斜杠。Unix 目录路径也要替换，例如使用 <code>'C:\\ProgramData\\OpenAI\\Codex\\models.json'</code>，并以管理员提供的实际路径为准。</p> <p>请单独配置 MCP 服务器和插件。模型网关凭据并不代表你获得了访问工具或已连接系统的授权。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-the-connection\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">验证连接</h2> <p>更改配置后，请重新启动客户端。在 CLI 中运行 <code>codex</code>，再使用 <code>/status</code> 检查当前启用的模型和提供商。在桌面应用中，检查所选模型和配置。</p> <p>在新任务中发送以下提示：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Reply with exactly: gateway-ok\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">只回复以下确切内容：gateway-ok</div></div> <p>预期结果为 <code>gateway-ok</code>。仅凭回复无法证明请求经过了哪条路由：请管理员确认网关记录的用户、模型别名和预期上游路由。不要通过询问模型名称来判断实际使用的模型。</p> <p>以上步骤只验证初始连接。管理员还应完成<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">部署检查</a>，验证流式输出、工具调用和后续轮次。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-the-connection\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">排查连接问题</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>现象</th> <th>检查内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>预期提供商未启用。</td> <td>检查所选配置文件和配置优先级。确认顶层键没有放在提供商表内部。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>身份验证失败。</td> <td>检查客户端进程是否能读取凭据变量，或已安装的助手是否能获取当前令牌。请管理员区分网关身份验证和上游身份验证问题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>找不到模型。</td> <td>确认管理员提供的模型名称，并请管理员检查对应路由。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>模型能力与预期不符。</td> <td>请管理员检查目录元数据是否与别名背后的模型相匹配。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>流式输出停滞或后续轮次失败。</td> <td>请网关负责人检查代理缓冲、终止事件 <code>response.completed</code> 和<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性</a>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>目录或助手路径无效。</td> <td>确认 Codex 运行环境中的配置绝对路径下确实存在该文件。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>寻求帮助时，请附上错误消息，并先移除令牌和敏感提示内容。</p> <p><a id=\"use-an-existing-gateway-deployment\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">使用现有网关部署</h2> <p>如果组织已将网关用于其他编码工具，可能可以复用其网络路径、日志记录和提供商访问。请与网关团队合作，配置并测试 Codex 连接：</p> <ol> <li>确认现有网关 URL、凭据机制、所需标头、模型路由和配置分发方式。</li> <li>请网关团队确认网关支持 <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Codex 所需的 API 行为</a>，并配置 Codex 模型路由。</li> <li>向网关团队获取具有限定作用域的网关凭据或凭据助手、模型名称，以及所需的模型目录。</li> <li>使用这些信息<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=configure-the-provider\">配置 Codex</a>。</li> <li>在计划使用的 CLI 或桌面应用中<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=verify-the-connection\">验证连接</a>。请网关团队完成<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">流式输出、工具调用和后续轮次检查</a>。</li> <li>试点验证通过后，请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">部署网关</a>向其他开发者分发配置。</li> </ol> <p>管理员迁移检查清单和配置映射请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=reuse-an-existing-gateway-deployment\">复用现有网关部署</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP 服务器</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"use-apiprovider-credentials-through-a-gateway\">Use API/provider credentials through a gateway</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Connect Codex to an LLM gateway using the gateway URL, model alias, and credential or token resolver your organization provides.</p> <p>To keep the gateway while signing in with a ChatGPT workspace, use <a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597\">Sign in with ChatGPT through a gateway</a>.</p> <p>For an organization-wide rollout, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">Roll out a gateway</a>. For the required API behavior, see <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility</a>. To connect directly to Bedrock without a gateway, see <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">Amazon Bedrock</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"check-for-an-existing-configuration\">Check for an existing configuration</h2> <p>Before adding anything, check whether your administrator already configured Codex.</p> <ul> <li>For the CLI, inspect the selected profile and run <code>codex doctor</code>. After startup, use <code>/status</code> to confirm the active model and provider.</li> <li>For the macOS app, inspect <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> or the managed configuration your organization delivers.</li> <li>For the Windows app, inspect <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\config.toml</code> or the system configuration your organization delivers.</li> </ul> <p>If the expected gateway provider and model are already active, continue to <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=verify-the-connection\">Verify the connection</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"get-your-gateway-connection-details\">Get your gateway connection details</h2> <p>Install the <a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a> or the desktop app approved by your organization. To configure Codex yourself, get these values from your gateway team:</p> <ul> <li>The HTTPS gateway base URL, including its API path, such as <code>https://gateway.example.com/v1</code>.</li> <li>The model name and provider ID to use.</li> <li>Your scoped gateway credential and its environment variable, or an installed token resolver and its configuration.</li> <li>Any required model catalog URL, or a catalog file and its absolute local path.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"configure-the-provider\">Configure the provider</h2> <p>Open <code>config.toml</code> at <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> on macOS or Linux, or <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\config.toml</code> on Windows.</p> <p>Merge this example into your existing configuration, replacing the URL and model with the values your administrator supplied. Don't add a second definition of an existing key or table. This example uses <code>gpt-6-sol</code>; use it without a custom catalog only if your administrator confirms that your Codex version recognizes the model and its bundled metadata matches the gateway.</p> <p>Keep <code>model</code>, <code>model_provider</code>, <code>model_catalog_json</code>, and <code>web_search</code> before the first TOML table. Keys placed after a table header belong to that table, so Codex won't read them as top-level settings.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"gpt-6-sol\"\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise-gateway\"\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]\nname = \"Organization Gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/v1\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\nenv_key = \"CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY\"\n</code></pre> <p>If your administrator supplies a catalog URL, add it to the existing <code>[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]</code> table:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_catalog_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/codex/models.json\"\n</code></pre> <p>Remove any effective <code>model_catalog_json</code> setting; it takes precedence over the URL. Administrators can find endpoint requirements in <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=serve-a-remote-catalog\">remote catalog setup</a>.</p> <p>If your administrator supplies a local model catalog file, save it and add <code>model_catalog_json</code> before the first TOML table, using the file's absolute path. Custom aliases need matching catalog metadata. For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_catalog_json = \"/etc/codex/gateway-models.json\"\n</code></pre> <p>Use the model name and catalog supplied together by your administrator. Don't add a catalog path unless the file exists at that location.</p> <p><code>enterprise-gateway</code> is an illustrative provider ID. Use the same ID in <code>model_provider</code>, <code>[model_providers.&lt;id&gt;]</code>, and <code>[model_providers.&lt;id&gt;.auth]</code>. This example disables web search for the initial connection test; your administrator should verify feature support before enabling it.</p> <p>Make your gateway credential available as <code>CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY</code> in the environment of the process that launches Codex, using your organization's secret delivery mechanism. Don't put the credential in TOML or a repository. A variable set in a terminal may not be available to an app launched from the desktop.</p> <h3 id=\"use-a-custom-authentication-header\">Use a custom authentication header</h3> <p>If your gateway requires a header such as <code>X-API-Key</code> instead of a bearer token, replace <code>env_key</code> in the provider table with:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">env_http_headers = { \"X-API-Key\" = \"CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY\" }\n</code></pre> <p>Use the exact header name your administrator provides. Codex reads the value from the named environment variable; keep the credential out of the configuration file. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">configuration reference</a> for <code>model_providers.&lt;id&gt;.env_http_headers</code>.</p> <p>If the custom header is your only authentication mechanism, use <code>model_catalog_json</code>; remote catalog discovery won't run.</p> <h3 id=\"use-an-organization-credential-helper\">Use an organization credential helper</h3> <p>If your administrator provides command-backed authentication, use their installed helper and configuration instead of <code>env_key</code>. Don't configure both mechanisms. The helper must exist on your machine; Codex doesn't install it. For example, replace the example <code>env_key</code> setting with this table, using the resolver path and arguments your administrator supplies:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[model_providers.enterprise-gateway.auth]\ncommand = \"/usr/local/bin/fetch-codex-gateway-token\"\nargs = [\"print-token\"]\ntimeout_ms = 30000\nrefresh_interval_ms = 300000\n</code></pre> <p>The <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">custom provider authentication reference</a> defines the command, arguments, timeout, refresh interval, and token output contract. Ask your administrator how to renew your sign-in if the helper can no longer retrieve a token.</p> <p>Use resolved absolute paths for helper executables and catalog files.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-the-cli\">Configure the CLI</h3> <p>The CLI reads <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> by default on macOS or Linux. After saving the provider settings, run <code>codex</code>. Inside WSL, use the Linux configuration and paths unless <code>CODEX_HOME</code> points elsewhere.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-the-macos-app\">Configure the macOS app</h3> <p>The macOS app reads the same <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>. After saving the provider settings, restart the app. If you use an environment variable for the credential, make sure it's available to the app process.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-the-windows-app\">Configure the Windows app</h3> <p>Place the provider settings in <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\config.toml</code>, then restart the app. For command-backed authentication, use the resolver installed by your administrator. For example, replace the Unix auth table with:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[model_providers.enterprise-gateway.auth]\ncommand = 'C:\\Program Files\\OpenAI\\Codex\\fetch-codex-gateway-token.exe'\nargs = [\"print-token\"]\ntimeout_ms = 30000\nrefresh_interval_ms = 300000\n</code></pre> <p>In Windows TOML, single-quoted literal strings preserve backslashes. Replace Unix catalog paths too, for example with <code>'C:\\ProgramData\\OpenAI\\Codex\\models.json'</code>, using the actual path your administrator supplied.</p> <p>Configure MCP servers and plugins separately. A model gateway credential doesn't authorize access to your tools or connected systems.</p> <h2 id=\"verify-the-connection\">Verify the connection</h2> <p>Restart the client after changing the configuration. In the CLI, start <code>codex</code> and use <code>/status</code> to inspect the active model and provider. In the desktop app, check the selected model and configuration.</p> <p>Send this prompt in a new task:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Reply with exactly: gateway-ok\n</code></pre> <p>Expect <code>gateway-ok</code>. A response alone doesn't prove which route handled it: ask your administrator to confirm that the gateway recorded your user, model alias, and intended upstream route. Don't identify the model by asking it its name.</p> <p>This verifies an initial connection. Administrators should also complete the <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">rollout checks</a> for streaming, tools, and follow-up turns.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshoot-the-connection\">Troubleshoot the connection</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Symptom</th> <th>What to check</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>The expected provider isn't active.</td> <td>Check the selected profile and configuration precedence. Confirm that top-level keys aren't inside a provider table.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Authentication fails.</td> <td>Check that the credential variable reaches the client process, or that the installed helper can retrieve a current token. Ask the administrator to distinguish gateway authentication from upstream authentication.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>The model isn't found.</td> <td>Confirm the supplied model name and ask the administrator to check its route.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>The model uses unexpected capabilities.</td> <td>Ask the administrator to check that the catalog metadata matches the model behind the alias.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Streaming stalls or follow-ups fail.</td> <td>Ask the gateway owner to check proxy buffering, the terminal <code>response.completed</code> event, and <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility</a>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A catalog or helper path fails.</td> <td>Confirm that the file exists at the configured absolute path in the environment running Codex.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>When requesting help, include the error message with tokens and sensitive prompts removed.</p> <h2 id=\"use-an-existing-gateway-deployment\">Use an existing gateway deployment</h2> <p>If your organization already uses a gateway with another coding tool, you may be able to reuse its network path, logging, and provider access. Work with your gateway team to configure and test a Codex connection:</p> <ol> <li>Identify the existing gateway URL, credential mechanism, required headers, model routes, and configuration delivery method.</li> <li>Ask your gateway team to confirm that the gateway supports the <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">API behavior Codex requires</a> and to configure a Codex model route.</li> <li>Obtain a scoped gateway credential or credential helper, the model name, and any required model catalog from your gateway team.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=configure-the-provider\">Configure Codex</a> with those values.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=verify-the-connection\">Verify the connection</a> in the CLI or desktop app you plan to use. Have your gateway team complete the <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">streaming, tool, and follow-up checks</a>.</li> <li>After the pilot passes, follow <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">Roll out a gateway</a> to distribute the configuration to other developers.</li> </ol> <p>For the administrator migration checklist and configuration mapping, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=reuse-an-existing-gateway-deployment\">Reuse an existing gateway deployment</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP servers</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul>"};
